{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 34, :comments ["<b>As one lying in the heart of the sea</b> — for he will think that he is encamped [at anchor] while he is sailing." "<b>חבל</b> — a noun, and it is the rope tied to the ship's iron. The meaning is that you will not feel the time of your anchoring and your sailing, and you will say: when the wine bites you, strike me, O strikers, and I will not know when I became ill from the blows."], :book :proverbs, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 23, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Proverbs -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/mishley/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:24:25.589714216Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}